-- title:
--   The cusp ∞ as a ℤ_{(ℓ)}-point of the pole chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) $\ell$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and $F$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull` $N$, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the $q$-expansions $q\mathrm{Expand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ j$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$. Let `chartAlgInf` $N\ \ell$ be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of $F$ whose elements are those $x \in F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by the single element $(jFull\ N)^{-1}$, the inverse in $F$ of the $q$-expansion of $j$. The assertion is that there exists a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgInf` $N\ \ell$ to $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ such that for every $x$ in that subalgebra the rational number underlying $\varphi(x)$ is the coefficient of $q^0$ in the Laurent series attached to $x$. In particular each such $x$ has $\ell$-integral constant coefficient, and $\varphi$ is pinned to be evaluation at $q = 0$.
--
--   This exhibits the cusp $\infty$ as a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-valued point of the chart of the Igusa scheme on which $1/j$ is regular, normalised so that it is evaluation of $q$-expansions at $q = 0$. It is used in the construction of the finite map data for the rational curve model of the Igusa scheme and in the verification of smoothness along the section at the cusp $\infty$.
